note omatmul.om: the Omega kernel behind the MAX CPU custom op "omega_matmul" (max-cpu/README.md).
note C[M,N] = A[M,K] @ B[K,N], row-major. A and B arrive as bfloat16 bit patterns in ONE view ab
note (A's M*K elements, then B's K*N): bf16 to f32 is exact (the 16 bits become the high half), each
note product of two bf16 values is exact in f32, and the K-term sum accumulates in f32 in order
note p = 0..K-1, one rounding per add (RNE, no fused multiply-add). C is written as f32 bit patterns.
note s holds the shape [M, K, N]. A, B and C cannot be three separate views because OM-2 function
note mode has six parameter slots and an unsized view takes two (spec/omegese-om2.md section 4).
note Result codes (status 0): 0 done; 1 a dimension is 0 or above 4096; 2 len ab is not M*K + K*N;
note 3 len c is not M*N. C is untouched unless the result is 0. Every index is also checked (trap 3).
om2
fn bdot ab view ushort * ai ulong bj ulong k ulong n ulong to uint
acc = f32 0.0
for p ulong k
x = bitcast f32 shl uint get ab add ai p 16
y = bitcast f32 shl uint get ab add bj mul p n 16
acc = add acc mul x y
end
ret bitcast uint acc
end
fn brow ab view ushort * c edit uint * s view ulong 3 i ulong to void
k = get s 1
n = get s 2
ka = mul get s 0 k
ai = mul i k
ci = mul i n
for j ulong n
put c add ci j bdot ab ai add ka j k n
end
end
export fn omatmul ab view ushort * c edit uint * s view ulong 3 to ulong
m = get s 0
k = get s 1
n = get s 2
if or or eq m 0 eq k 0 eq n 0
ret 1
end
if or or gt m 4096 gt k 4096 gt n 4096
ret 1
end
ka = mul m k
if ne len ab add ka mul k n
ret 2
end
if ne len c mul m n
ret 3
end
for i ulong m
brow ab c s i
end
ret 0
end
